<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vlastimir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 830–850</span> · Also known as Vlastimir of Serbia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vlastimir was Prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> in the first half of the 9th century and the ruler who gave his name to the Vlastimirović dynasty. He united several Serbian tribes and defeated the Bulgarian khan Presian in a three-year war around 839 to 842. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-vii">Constantine VII</a> records that he married his daughter to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krajina">Krajina</a>, ruler of Travunia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vlastimir.jpg" alt="Vlastimir" width="320" height="436" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zoupan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vlastimir,_Prince_of_the_Serbs.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
